  "body": "## Result\n\nFor M=[[1,1,1],[1,1,-1],[1,-1,0]], exactly twelve ordinary signed Ai/Bj queries and four nonzero arbitrary Q/C scalar shears on two independent dirty roots admit **no mixed-direction transfer word**. Combined with credited PR1983/PR1651, the entire bidirectional four-pass class reduces to the two global one-way forced-unit/forced-port classes. Its complete additive tariff is the minimum of their two fully priced sums.\n\nThis closes PR1675\u2019s explicit four-pass handoff. It does not claim a new four-pass minimum or construction: PR1675 excludes <=3; PR1651 attains4; PR1682 and PR1983 prove the unit and arbitrary-coefficient one-way results. Those predecessors remain unchanged and credited.\n\n## Why this covers arbitrary coefficients\n\nThe symbolic root-only classification reduces every restoring mixed four-shear word, using centrality and cyclic rotation of the full endpoint, to U(a),U(-a),L(b),L(-b). Exact normalized source columns and dirty reader rows permit a port-changing pair only when a=b=+1 or a=b=-1. Outside those cases, cross-root coefficients vanish and connected target support reduces to the inherited one-root obstruction.\n\nThe exceptional cases reduce to one unit loop, with **all eight column-sign choices and both source/read port changes retained**. Chronological propagation and a separate phase-placement/open-interval checker agree on every full 27-bit reader mask for all69,948 canonical source traces /559,584 signed traces. There are7,020 canonical source-port-changing traces and zero target successes. An all-ones target has51,192 successes; explicit legal source-switch/read-switch pilots prevent an invalid reuse of the old same-port assumption.\n\n## Evidence and reproduction\n\nOnly `research/bidirectional-four-shear-rigidity/` changes: complete proof, exact evidence, two checker models, meaningful semantic/binding controls, source pins, full chooser selection, TASK, VERIFY and exercised validation.\n\n```sh\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python scripts/research_package.py --package research/bidirectional-four-shear-rigidity\n```\n\nObserved on CPython3.12.12/macOS arm64:\n- `PASS_BIDIRECTIONAL_FOUR_SHEAR_RIGIDITY canonical_traces=69948 signed_traces=559584 mixed_successes=0 symbolic_shapes=16 no_new_kappa`\n- `PASS_FOUR_SHEAR_PACKAGE_CONTROLS source_mutations=5 receipt_mutations=1 relocated_optimized=true read_only=true`\n- `PASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE ... outcome=negative-result`\n\nThe parent independently reviewed the reduction and replayed this registered package before publication. No hosted CI success is claimed.\n\n## Scope, attribution and independent assignment\n\nNo physical supplier, new recursive moment/kappa, proof-assistant acceptance, selected cold replay, or new full child lowering is claimed. Scratch restoration is the complete-query interface premise. Both checker algorithms were written by the same AI assistant, not independent humans.\n\nCredit Ross Richardson (PR944/943/934,1651,1682), Charles Bethin (PR1637,1983), Cinna Davis (PR1675), and their retained lineage. New work: Adam Gall with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance; Apache-2.0.\n\nSingle independent seed `652b2d372ee11d8364eb3ba12820c34c`; recursive-interfaces / connector-alphabet-change; base `e112d71c8d7bb32435debcc54df932593dd8223a`; no reroll. Claim: #research-claim-and-completion-record . Final overlap used complete343-open-PR/717-discussion shared snapshot plus targeted live/merged predecessors; no-match is not a novelty proof. PR2065\u2019s F2 five-source/six-transfer result is distinct.\n\nFull commit: `ac135d637e74dd11d44901bc91863f2990823e59`.\n\n## Research claim and completion record\n\nStatus: completed. The claim record is preserved here so this PR is self-contained. Historical coordination links in the committed research metadata refer to this record; the separate coordination discussion is being removed.\n\nDONE \u2014 seed652b2d372ee11d8364eb3ba12820c34c; recursive-interfaces / connector-alphabet-change. [PR2071](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2071), full commit ac135d637e74dd11d44901bc91863f2990823e59, based on e112d71c8d7bb32435debcc54df932593dd8223a. Claim released.\n\nResult: for signed M=[[1,1,1],[1,1,-1],[1,-1,0]], exactly12 ordinary signed Ai/Bj queries and4 nonzero arbitrary Q/C root shears admit no mixed-direction word. Thus the whole bidirectional four-pass class reduces to the two global one-way forced-unit/forced-port classes of credited PR1983/1651, and its additive tariff is the minimum of their two complete sums.\n\nCritical reduction: all mixed restoring4shear loops are disjoint/nested inverse excursions; endpoint centrality permits rotation to U(a),U(-a),L(b),L(-b). Genuine port switches force a=b=\u00b11. All other cases have zero cross-root coefficients and collapse to the inherited one-root obstruction. Both exact exceptional-case engines include source/read port changes and all8column-sign choices:69948canonical/559584signed traces,7020 source-switch traces,zero target successes;51192 all-ones positive-control successes. Full reader-mask maps agree, not merely totals.\n\nFocused smoke and registered CPython3.12 replay passed, including symbolic checks, dirty-state/inverse/rotation controls,5actualsource corruptions,1receiptcorruption and relocated optimized read-only replay. Parent separately reviewed and replayed before publication. Reproduce with `uv run --python 3.12 --no-project python scripts/research_package.py --package research/bidirectional-four-shear-rigidity`.\n\nCredit Cinna Davis PR1675 for <=3bidirectional exclusion and this explicit4pass handoff; Ross Richardson PR944 target,PR1651 witness,PR1682 one-way port theorem; Charles Bethin PR1637 and PR1983 arbitrary-coefficient one-way theorem. The four-pass minimum and attaining circuit are not new here. No physical supplier, new kappa, formal-kernel acceptance, fullchildlowering or hostedCI success is claimed. Adam Gall with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance; Apache-2.0.\n\nOriginal scope before computation: classify all arbitrary-coefficient mixed-direction restoring4shear loops and jointly solve the paired source/read constraints at the fixed12query signed target; price every actual-port query, root pass, admission, preparation, routing, precision and control. TASK and complete SELECTION preserve the independent draw and bound. No reroll or mathematical coordination; final shared343PR/717discussion snapshot and targeted live/merged predecessors checked.\n",
